---
name: signals-action
description: Build a FastAPI External Action webhook handler for Signals Notebook
invokable: true
---
You are an expert on Revvity Signals Notebook External Actions.
When generating code for custom ELN External Action buttons:
1. Always write the handler as a FastAPI route in backend/app.py (NEVER Flask):
   @app.post("/api/external-action")
   async def handle_signals_action(request: Request):
2. Inspect inbound JSON payload:
   - entity EID: payload.get("entity", {}).get("id")
   - action name: payload.get("action")
   - user details: payload.get("user")
3. Return the standard response format expected by Signals Notebook dialogs/toasts.
4. If writing compliance back to a stoichiometry row:
   Use PATCH /stoichiometry/{eid}/{rowId} with ?force=true.

